            <div xml:id="d682">

                <pb facs="0603" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1735: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Berle</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the President of the Foreign Bondholders Protective
                        Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-05">March 5, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Have requested Caffery to try to hold matters open pending our receipt of further
                    word from you.</p>
                <p>The Department’s position is that it has obtained the best offer possible. The
                    Council’s decision as to the course it follows must be exclusively its own
                    responsibility. The Department believes it should not accept your telephone
                    communication in view of the fact that you coupled it with the statement that it
                    was taken only on the assumption that Department had requested such action.</p>
                <closer><signed>A. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
